        "original_id": "17865727-6692-5def-8ace-c06984fb205d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am)\"\n- People: Ray Whitley, Rick Hall\n- Groups: The Tams\n- Organizations: FAME Studios, Alabama Music Hall of Fame\n- Places: Muscle Shoals, Alabama\n- Awards: John Herbert Orr Pioneer Award\n\nFacts:\n- \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am)\" is a 1964 single written by Ray Whitley and recorded by The Tams.\n- FAME Studios in Muscle Shoals, Alabama, recorded \"What Kind of Fool (Do You Think I Am)\" as one of its many hit records.\n- Rick Hall was inducted into the Alabama Music Hall of Fame in 1985.\n- Rick Hall also received the John Herbert Orr Pioneer Award.",
